    # formatting.md, "P2": "The negative log through the binary: --cf-sample on
    # a fixture whose one rule holds an extLst on the cell the sample removes
    # (refused) and on one whose kept rule's priority is not a number (refused),
    # each with a control."). One family, the gate's host debug binary copied
    # into a detached worktree of the phase commit and checked against
    # gate.log's hash, on fictional packages this log builds from the phase
    # commit's template files. The template's worksheet holds an empty sheetData
    # alone, so M is 0: the sample's rules go on A1:C1 and A2, and it removes the
    # format on A2 again. The template's styles part has no dxfs, so the
    # sample's differential style creates one before the root's end tag:
    #
    # (C) --cf-sample, the template's worksheet children after its empty
    #     sheetData set per case:
    #       C0 the bare template, no conditional format: exit 0, its line;
    #       C1 one conditionalFormatting on A2 whose one dataBar rule holds an
    #          extLst: the sample's removal of A2 meets the extension message,
    #          after the output was written, so the tool removes it;
    #       C2 the same element on D1, the control for C1: exit 0, its line;
    #       C3 one conditionalFormatting on D1 whose one expression rule's
    #          priority is "high", not a number: the ruling-4 message, at the
    #          read of the input's rules;
    #       C4 the same rule with priority "1", the control for C3: exit 0, its
    #          line;
    #       C5 the template's styles part with two empty <dxfs/> before its
    #          end tag (the worksheet bare): the two-dxfs message at the
    #          differential style's call, reachable through the binary, so run
    #          (control C0).
    # Each refusal: exit 2, the error line exactly the message the committed
    # source holds, no stdout, no output file. Then the messages of this phase,
    # read from the source by constant name, compared as SETS with those reached
    # here and those the log states unreachable, with the reason for each; and
    # usage shapes.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M2 part 4b P2 from P1's negative script (printed in
    # records/logs/m2p4b-p1/negative.log; its change list AC to AG is there,
    # and specs/0020's P1 verification rulings add nothing to this log). Grepped
    # for P1's tokens in every form (p1, validate, dataValidation, V0 to V4,
    # dc4cb485, the P1 subjects and commits). What differs, and why:
    #  AH. The phase, the log directory, the subjects and the build directories
    #      are part 4b P2's. The base is P1's record commit ("M2 part 4b P1
    #      record:"); the doc commit and the four code commits by their full P2
    #      subjects. This script lives on the disk in the phase's scripts
    #      directory under the home directory's .cache/emend-build/m2p4b-p2,
    #      shown as <scripts>, with its standard error in <scripts>/out. The
    #      gate's log and build directory default to
    #      records/logs/m2p4b-p2/gate.log and the phase's gate directory; both
    #      are labelled input lines.
    #  AI. The family is C0 to C5 above, the generator gen-c.py editing the
    #      template's worksheet right after its empty sheetData, and for C5 the
    #      styles part before its end tag.
    #  AJ. The messages of this phase are the constants from DXF_FIELD to
    #      RULE_UNPARSED in the source, read by constant name, each checked
    #      non-empty, and that set compared with the reached and the
    #      stated-unreachable ones.
    #  AK. The spec. The log pins the COMMITTED spec: the blob at the phase
    #      commit (P2's doc commit's) at
    #      95daff46e164f3552df4aff671d800a31347fde40319fc1667bc9aba75900d8d.
    #      The working file differs: it holds planning's uncommitted "Planning
